From 7468ca0cf86c0b5f3cdc212425fef0160825d50c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:48:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 074/211] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: add CPU DVFS support

Add the CPU clock controller, the SID with the DVFS code and the
operating points of both clusters, taken from the vendor tables for a
26 MHz oscillator.

The DSU shares the little cluster supply and has no scaling of its own
yet, so it is parked at 780 MHz, the highest rate every speed bin runs at
the lowest voltage of that supply. Boot firmware leaves it at whatever it
picked for the cores, which is not safe once the cores scale down.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
